## Gotchas learned (carry into the next port)

- **Bundled assets don't come for free.** iOS bundles JSON in the app bundle; on
  Android every catalog, schema, and other JSON the iOS app reads must be copied
  to `app/src/main/assets/` and read via the `AssetManager`. Shipping screens
  before those files makes the feature fail with a `FileNotFoundException`
  *before the network call*, and a generic error sheet hides the cause. **Add a
  test in Phase 3a that loads every bundled asset and decodes it.**
- **Never swallow exceptions silently.** The generation catch block showed a generic
  sheet with no log, which hid the real cause. Always `Log.e(tag, msg, e)` before
  presenting a user-facing error.
- **Enum decoding must be total.** `kotlinx.serialization` throws on any enum value
  not present in the Kotlin enum (unlike a lenient string). Give dataset-backed enums
  a custom serializer with a `fromRaw(...) -> UNKNOWN` fallback, or the whole list
  decode fails on a single stray value.
- **Firestore merge writes:** omit `null` optional fields from the map in `LiveFirestoreRemoteStore` or you clobber
  remote data (the equivalent of Swift's `encodeIfPresent`).
- **Never overwrite Firestore with a corrupted local blob fallback.** If Room JSON decoding fails, log via `Log.e`, set `hasBlobDecodeError = true`, and re-hydrate from Firestore (`syncMostRecentFromFirestoreToRoom`) — block `saveToFirestore` from pushing `.default` to the cloud.
- **Case-insensitive filesystem:** renaming a file only by case (`AppUiState` →
  `AppUIState`) needs `git mv -f`, and watch for stray `Foo 2.kt` duplicates that
  compile via cache but break a clean build.
- **Confirm the callable contract early:** function name, region (`us-central1`
  default on both platforms), payload shape, and whether App Check / auth are
  enforced. All four are common "works on iOS, fails on Android" causes.
- **Play listing is not an API call.** Copy `android-play/` into `tools/play/`
  during Phase 6, but the first app record, questionnaires, and Play App Signing
  enrollment stay in the Console. Service-account invites can take a few hours
  before `play whoami` works.

## Rough effort total

Phase 0 (kickoff alignment & inventory): **~0.5 hr**. Phases 1–5 (logic, Dual-Write data, services, coordinator, screens): **~14–18 hrs** of focused
build time, plus toolchain setup. Phase 6 (polish + release): **~3–4 hrs** of build
work, with the store/release steps gated on producer assets and device QA.
